# Cline Rules for SeeThrough Project

## TypeORM Entity Relations

Every TypeORM entity relation field decorated with @ManyToOne, @OneToMany, @OneToOne, or @ManyToMany MUST use the `Relation<T>` wrapper type from `typeorm` instead of just `T`, where `T` is the relation entity type.

```typescript
// CORRECT
import { type Relation } from 'typeorm';

@ManyToOne(() => User, (user) => user.sessions, { onDelete: 'CASCADE' })
user: Relation<User>;

@OneToMany(() => Session, (session) => session.user)
sessions: Relation<Session[]>;
```

```typescript
// WRONG - do NOT do this
@ManyToOne(() => User, (user) => user.sessions, { onDelete: 'CASCADE' })
user: User;

@OneToMany(() => Session, (session) => session.user)
sessions: Session[];
```

This ensures proper type safety when working with TypeORM's lazy/loaded relations.

## ActiveRecord Pattern

Always use TypeORM's ActiveRecord pattern. All entities extend `BaseEntity`, giving them static methods for database operations. Use these directly on entity classes instead of injecting repositories via `@InjectRepository`.

The root `TypeOrmModule.forRootAsync` already has `autoLoadEntities: true`, so `TypeOrmModule.forFeature()` is unnecessary and should NOT be used.

```typescript
// CORRECT — static methods on entity classes:
const user = await User.findOneBy({ id: userId });
const role = Role.create({ name: 'admin', permissions: [] });
await role.save();
await user.remove();
const count = await User.count({ where: { active: true } });

// For complex queries:
const result = await UserMfa.createQueryBuilder('mfa')
  .addSelect(['mfa.secret'])
  .where({ id: enrollmentId })
  .getOne();
```

```typescript
// WRONG — do NOT inject repositories:
import { InjectRepository } from '@nestjs/typeorm';
import { Repository } from 'typeorm';

constructor(
  @InjectRepository(User)
  private readonly userRepo: Repository<User>,
) {}

// then later:
this.userRepo.findOneBy({ id: userId });
this.userRepo.create({ ... });
```

```typescript
// WRONG — do NOT use TypeOrmModule.forFeature():
import { TypeOrmModule } from '@nestjs/typeorm';

@Module({
  imports: [
    TypeOrmModule.forFeature([User, Session, Role]),
  ],
})
```

This keeps the code concise and avoids unnecessary dependency injection for database operations.
